e same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{21}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{21}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 12 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 5 & -6\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d6055d74-81b9-54e0-8fc3-55044161a211"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d6055d74-81b9-54e0-8fc3-55044161a211" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6055d74-81b9-54e0-8fc3-55044161a211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c4eb8721-33ec-52bc-8a6e-8bb24d93b164" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4eb8721-33ec-52bc-8a6e-8bb24d93b164" "answer-24b9de88-7ddb-5b58-b30d-923571de9446" "answer-d00d7ab2-12e5-5af5-a41f-707d9c669240" "answer-d0a38a5e-bb09-5bb9-acfc-39240d600c3b" "answer-78242538-3ed6-59de-be3c-33fa32cdeeb5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4eb8721-33ec-52bc-8a6e-8bb24d93b164" :answer/id #uuid "c4eb8721-33ec-52bc-8a6e-8bb24d93b164" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-24b9de88-7ddb-5b58-b30d-923571de9446" :answer/id #uuid "24b9de88-7ddb-5b58-b30d-923571de9446" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 10 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d00d7ab2-12e5-5af5-a41f-707d9c669240" :answer/id #uuid "d00d7ab2-12e5-5af5-a41f-707d9c669240" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0a38a5e-bb09-5bb9-acfc-39240d600c3b" :answer/id #uuid "d0a38a5e-bb09-5bb9-acfc-39240d600c3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -8\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78242538-3ed6-59de-be3c-33fa32cdeeb5" :answer/id #uuid "78242538-3ed6-59de-be3c-33fa32cdeeb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3010fec5-ce32-5d13-98b7-fb9085f51f6f" :question/id #uuid "3010fec5-ce32-5d13-98b7-fb9085f51f6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-91252" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 & 5\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{11}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{11}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 & 5\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 9 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(3-45) \\\\  & =126.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eb0d831e-6e0f-59da-ab3f-8c9921b69fc6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb0d831e-6e0f-59da-ab3f-8c9921b69fc6" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0d831e-6e0f-59da-ab3f-8c9921b69fc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e73e510a-6138-525f-beef-ac3b1cf34f5a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2a376ea-df94-535c-826d-ac17d1f3a3ce" "answer-a328cadc-7951-533e-ad43-d926e5950f13" "answer-d15147b2-fac5-5c6f-b4db-ec70e4487643" "answer-e73e510a-6138-525f-beef-ac3b1cf34f5a" "answer-8d041347-974c-5211-8af3-0d1eb0d54714"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2a376ea-df94-535c-826d-ac17d1f3a3ce" :answer/id #uuid "d2a376ea-df94-535c-826d-ac17d1f3a3ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a328cadc-7951-533e-ad43-d926e5950f13" :answer/id #uuid "a328cadc-7951-533e-ad43-d926e5950f13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d15147b2-fac5-5c6f-b4db-ec70e4487643" :answer/id #uuid "d15147b2-fac5-5c6f-b4db-ec70e4487643" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e73e510a-6138-525f-beef-ac3b1cf34f5a" :answer/id #uuid "e73e510a-6138-525f-beef-ac3b1cf34f5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "126" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d041347-974c-5211-8af3-0d1eb0d54714" :answer/id #uuid "8d041347-974c-5211-8af3-0d1eb0d54714" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a480ef82-6feb-5a68-8ebb-ae39b1e1fdd6" :question/id #uuid "a480ef82-6feb-5a68-8ebb-ae39b1e1fdd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-132164" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & -12 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 7 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{21}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{21}=2$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & -12 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -2 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 7 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+3{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -5 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -5 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (3)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-6(-24+25) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1f9d5e5b-5991-59ed-8d72-899297761d31"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1f9d5e5b-5991-59ed-8d72-899297761d31" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f9d5e5b-5991-59ed-8d72-899297761d31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a430a60c-83ee-5d5c-8cf4-6a744fbb05e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a430a60c-83ee-5d5c-8cf4-6a744fbb05e1" "answer-7ea7ed90-4e78-5c2d-b342-fa5379b66c60" "answer-15adda79-ba8c-5250-86b2-2c890fbe9191" "answer-077a1997-2530-5fe1-b114-aa83cbfd33fd" "answer-d4d4f963-ecf8-5d50-9b3a-1d7bb8cdd506"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a430a60c-83ee-5d5c-8cf4-6a744fbb05e1" :answer/id #uuid "a430a60c-83ee-5d5c-8cf4-6a744fbb05e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ea7ed90-4e78-5c2d-b342-fa5379b66c60" :answer/id #uuid "7ea7ed90-4e78-5c2d-b342-fa5379b66c60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15adda79-ba8c-5250-86b2-2c890fbe9191" :answer/id #uuid "15adda79-ba8c-5250-86b2-2c890fbe9191" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-077a1997-2530-5fe1-b114-aa83cbfd33fd" :answer/id #uuid "077a1997-2530-5fe1-b114-aa83cbfd33fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4d4f963-ecf8-5d50-9b3a-1d7bb8cdd506" :answer/id #uuid "d4d4f963-ecf8-5d50-9b3a-1d7bb8cdd506" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120419 :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below ${a}_{11}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary row operations, let's make entries below ${a}_{11}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4-(-2)) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118628 :answer-field/correct 17592186118632 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186121046 :tutorial/content "One way to simplify a determinant calculation is to create a row (or column) containing all zeros except for one entry. Then, we can use a Laplace expansion across that row (or column) to compute the determinant.\n\nLet's demonstrate this method on the matrix $A$ below.\n\n![](images/37/37946204f088b803603ba8adc3f93494e1d49fbe59d9c0925347675311b23e5d.svg)\n\nNotice that we can make entries to the right of $a_{21}=1$ equal to zero using elementary *column* operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one column to another column in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 14 & 17\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(21-10) \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119995 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
